debook to bringing up young people I  suppose  and he does it as a persona as a  description of his own use and success  I don't know I think that what you see  in Franklin is what you get you get what  you see in Franklin he won't give you  everything but what he gives you is is  straight it's not something that's  constructed deliberately as much as as  many English scholars seem to think  edmond morgan is a history professor at  yale university for more information on  Benjamin Franklin visit Yale University  Press online at yale.edu slash
 

